<item>
            <title>[LU-20916]  fix --enable-gss detection in dkms conf</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20916</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The DKMS configuration checks for &quot;--enable-gss&quot; in the configure&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;options using the regex &apos;--enable-gss&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;^-&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&apos;. This requires a character&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;after &quot;gss&quot;, so it fails to match when &quot;--enable-gss&quot; is the last&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;argument in the options string, and ptlrpc_gss is silently omitted&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;from the DKMS module list.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Change the regex to &apos;--enable-gss($|&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;^-&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;)&apos; so that it matches at end&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;of string as well, while still excluding longer options such as&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&quot;--enable-gss-keyring&quot; or &quot;-enable-gss-foo&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Apply the fix to both debian/dkms.conf.in and&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lustre/scripts/dkms.mkconf.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
